      "abstract": "Abstract In most his most recent accounts of European integration, J.H.H. Weiler claims that Europe was built with Messianic fervour. After the destruction and evil wrought by the Second World War, Europe was supposed to be a \u2018promised land\u2019. The article examines how Weiler conflates the narrative of the exodus with the Messianic leap into a different aeon and concludes that they have to be held distinct. It also suggests that Weiler\u2019s fusion of two distinct religious ideas betrays the force of \u2018Europe\u2019 as an \u2018empty signifier\u2019 (Laclau) of integration.",
